window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-ad27af11feac2791"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-a-lesson-deck\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">制作课程演示文稿</h1> <p>把已批准的教学材料整理成可编辑的演示文稿。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT，根据经审核的单元计划、既有幻灯片或笔记、学区模板、已批准的图片和无障碍要求，制作原生格式的课程演示文稿，并附上演讲者备注、理解检查和来源标注。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>要把已批准教案制作为精良演示文稿的教师。</li> <li>必须遵循学区模板和无障碍指导的演示文稿。</li> <li>需要演讲者备注、形成性检查和来源引用的课程。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>收集经审核的单元计划、已批准的来源、图片和学区模板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>制作原生格式、可编辑的课程演示文稿。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>制作课程演示文稿</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用此文件夹中的经审核单元计划、已批准的来源材料、图片和学区模板，为 [lesson] 制作一份原生格式、可编辑的 Google Slides 演示文稿。\n\n请包括：\n- 一个开场问题\n- 简明的讲解\n- 完整示范的例题\n- 两个理解检查\n- 一项离堂检核\n- 演讲者备注\n- 来源标注\n\n请遵循我提供的无障碍要求。保持演示文稿可编辑，并标明“草稿，供教师审核”。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-from-reviewed-content\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">从已审核的内容开始</h2> <p>使用已批准的单元或课程计划、当前来源材料、学区演示文稿模板、已批准的图片和无障碍要求。将来源内容与可选示例区分开。</p> <p>清楚的来源优先级可以避免过时的幻灯片取代已经审核过的计划。</p> <p><a id=\"build-the-presentation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">制作演示文稿</h2> <p>请 ChatGPT 制作一份结构连贯、原生格式且可编辑的演示文稿，其中包括：</p> <ul> <li>开场问题或现象</li> <li>简明讲解</li> <li>完整示范的例题</li> <li>理解检查</li> <li>练习或讨论提示</li> <li>离堂检核</li> <li>演讲者备注</li> <li>来源标注</li> </ul> <p>演示文稿应支持教学，而不是把每个细节都塞进幻灯片文字中。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-the-native-deck\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">检查原生演示文稿</h2> <p>请检查实际演示文稿，而不只是大纲。核对可读性、节奏、无障碍性、图片使用权限、来源准确性，以及备注是否包含教师所需的细节。</p> <p>分阶段、有针对性地修改。在教师确认内容和教学顺序可以使用之前，请始终将它标记为草稿。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-a-lesson-deck\">Create a lesson deck</h1> <p>Turn approved teaching materials into an editable presentation.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with a reviewed unit plan, prior slides or notes, a district template, approved images, and accessibility requirements to create a native lesson deck with speaker notes, checks for understanding, and source attribution.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teachers turning an approved lesson plan into a polished deck.</li> <li>Presentations that must follow a district template and accessibility guidance.</li> <li>Lessons that need speaker notes, formative checks, and citations.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Gather the reviewed unit plan, approved sources, images, and district template.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>Create a native, editable lesson presentation.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create a Lesson Deck</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a native Google Slides deck for [lesson] using the reviewed unit plan, approved source materials, images, and district template in this folder.\n\nInclude:\n- an opening question\n- concise explanations\n- worked examples\n- two checks for understanding\n- an exit ticket\n- speaker notes\n- source attribution\n\nFollow the accessibility requirements I provide. Keep the deck editable and label it Draft for educator review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-from-reviewed-content\">Start from reviewed content</h2> <p>Use an approved unit or lesson plan, current source materials, a district presentation template, approved images, and accessibility requirements. Separate source content from optional examples.</p> <p>A clear source hierarchy prevents outdated slides from overriding the reviewed plan.</p> <h2 id=\"build-the-presentation\">Build the presentation</h2> <p>Ask ChatGPT to create a native, editable deck with a coherent lesson flow:</p> <ul> <li>opening question or phenomenon</li> <li>concise instruction</li> <li>worked examples</li> <li>checks for understanding</li> <li>practice or discussion prompts</li> <li>exit ticket</li> <li>speaker notes</li> <li>source attribution</li> </ul> <p>The deck should support instruction rather than turn every detail into slide text.</p> <h2 id=\"inspect-the-native-deck\">Inspect the native deck</h2> <p>Review the actual presentation, not only an outline. Check readability, pacing, accessibility, image permissions, source accuracy, and whether notes contain the detail the teacher needs.</p> <p>Revise the deck in focused passes. Keep it labeled as a draft until an educator confirms that the content and instructional sequence are ready to use.</p>"};
